  "summary": "Decorated barkcloth created from wauke (paper mulberry) bark through beating and watermarking techniques.",
  "description": "Features distinctive watermark patterns (komo) created by beating with grooved mallets, often combined with freehand painting in natural dyes. Reflects Hawaiian cosmology and was used for clothing, bedding, and ceremonial purposes.",
